Here’s a McKinsey-style SCQA storyboard (10+ slides) tailored to your AI-driven self-serve analytical intelligence platform (based on your problem + vertical context). This is structured the way consulting firms expect: sharp headlines (so what), clear logic flow, and slide-level content.
Slide 1 — Title Slide
Headline:
AI-Powered Self-Serve Analytics: Reducing Decision Latency from Days to Seconds
Content:
Team details
Context: Payments / Banking / FinServ
Objective: Democratize analytics using AI
Slide 2 — Situation
Headline:
Businesses operate in data-rich environments but rely on centralized analytics teams
Content:
Payments & banking generate millions of transactions daily
Decision-making depends on data insights (success rates, fraud signals, revenue)
Analytics is currently centralized in data teams
Tools like Tableau/Power BI require:
Pre-built dashboards
SQL knowledge
Result: Business users cannot independently explore data
Slide 3 — Complication
Headline:
Centralized analytics creates bottlenecks, slowing critical business decisions
Content:
Analytics requests take 5–7 business days
Heavy backlog of tickets
Multiple inefficiencies:
Translation loss (business → analyst → SQL)
Iterative back-and-forth
Limited analyst bandwidth
In payments:
Delayed response to failure spikes
Missed real-time issue detection
In banking:
Slow risk/fraud insights
Delayed compliance reporting
Slide 4 — Key Question
Headline:
How can businesses enable instant, accurate, and governed analytics without relying on data teams?
Content:
Key requirements:
Natural language interface
Real-time query execution
Business-context understanding
Governance & compliance
Core question:
“Can analytics be as simple as asking a question?”
Slide 5 — Answer (Solution Overview)
Headline:
An AI-driven self-serve analytics platform enables users to query data in natural language
Content:
Users ask questions like:
“Why did success rate drop today?”
“Which gateway is failing most?”
System capabilities:
NL → SQL translation
Hypothesis-driven analysis
Automated visualization
Governed outputs
Slide 6 — How It Works (Architecture)
Headline:
The platform combines NL understanding, semantic mapping, and autonomous analytics
Content:
Input Layer:
Natural language query
Data catalog & schema
Business glossary
Governance rules
Processing Layer:
NL2SQL engine
Hypothesis generator
Query optimizer
Output Layer:
Direct answer
Charts
SQL + reasoning trace
Slide 7 — Key Capabilities
Headline:
The system delivers four core capabilities beyond traditional BI tools
Content:
Natural Language Interface
No SQL required
Business-friendly
Autonomous Analytics
Generates multiple hypotheses
Performs root cause analysis
Decision Intelligence
Provides answers, not just dashboards
Governance Layer
Row-level security
PII masking
Audit trails
